From ba8c67e0b15b2a33f69b954838249890ed9259a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:06:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Recover mean_density for checkpoints of models without LDA
 readouts

migrate_model_state_dict returned early when a state held no
readout.<i>.mean_density entries, so a training checkpoint written before
model file format 2 for a model without LDA readouts failed the strict
load with a missing model-level mean_density. The scale is now recovered
whenever the model expects it and the state lacks it: from
a_features.mean_density (the CACE scale the model copies at construction),
falling back to agreeing LDA readout copies when there is no feature
module. Readout copies are still dropped, every recorded scale must agree,
and loading stays strict.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CKJKJnMQ5g5crBBPsN5iZn
